  "title": "Fixed-point logic with counting",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Question Can either of the following be expressed in fixed-point logic plus counting:\n\n- Given a graph, does it have a perfect matching, i.e., a set $M$ of edges such that every vertex is incident to exactly one edge from $M$?\n- Given a square matrix over a finite field (regarded as a structure in the natural way, as described in [BGS02]), what is its determinant?",
